diff --git i/README.md w/README.md
index 17db3ec..679e5cd 100644
--- i/README.md
+++ w/README.md
@@ -18,6 +18,14 @@ Both halves work now, at the same time:
 Tested on a MacBookPro13,2 running Omarchy (Arch), kernel 7.1.9, LUKS2+Btrfs,
 SDDM + Hyprland.
 
+The shipped `kernel/appletbdrm.c` tracks stock Linux **7.2**. Linux 7.2 changed
+the DRM plane-helper API (`atomic_check`/`atomic_update` take a
+`drm_atomic_commit`, and the damage bookkeeping moved into `begin_fb_access`),
+so the 7.1-based file fails to build on 7.2 kernels with incompatible-pointer
+errors in the plane helper funcs. The T1 patch itself,
+`kernel/patches/appletbdrm-t1.patch`, is untouched by that change and applies
+to both the 7.1 and 7.2 stock sources.
+
 ---
 
 ## Why this was thought impossible
@@ -191,6 +199,7 @@ to its defaults, so run it after editing.
 |---|---|---|
 | `pacman -Syu` / `omarchy update` | none — every installed file is unowned by any package | — |
 | kernel update | DKMS rebuilds `appletbdrm-t1` | DKMS autoinstall |
+| kernel update changes a DRM or HID API | the DKMS build fails and the panel stays dark after the next boot | re-apply `kernel/patches/appletbdrm-t1.patch` to the new kernel's stock `drivers/gpu/drm/tiny/appletbdrm.c`, copy the result to `kernel/appletbdrm.c`, re-run `install.sh` |
 | kernel update renumbers `MT_CLS_APPLE_TOUCHBAR` | would silently bind the wrong class | `touchbar-t1-setup` reads the value out of the installed `hid-multitouch` at runtime instead of hardcoding it |
 | **systemd update** | our `71-seat.rules` shadows the new stock file and silently pins the old one | pacman hook regenerates it; `doctor.sh` flags staleness by mtime |
 | distro packages `tiny-dfr` | would install `/usr/bin/tiny-dfr` unpatched, alongside ours in `/usr/local/bin` | `doctor.sh` checks the running binary carries the name patch |
